  "historyNote": "#14388, eff 10-24-25, EXPIRES: 10-24-35",
  "inScheme": "https://granitestate.github.io/rules/scheme",
  "notation": "Plc 2003.02",
  "officialHtml": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/plc2000.html",
  "prefLabel": "Plc 2003.02 Qualifying Based on Work Experience",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Plc 2003.02 Qualifying Based on Work Experience.\n\n(a) An individual shall be deemed qualified for certification as a CHW if the individual has not less than 4,000 hours of work experience, obtained in the past 5 years, that fall within the scope of practice of a CHW as defined by the National Council of CHW Core Consensus Standards (National C3 Council) at https://www.c3council.org/roles-competencies.\n\n(b) Both paid and unpaid work experience shall count towards the total hours required.\n\n(c) Only hours engaged in work that falls within the CHW scope of practice, hereinafter “qualifying duties”, shall count towards the total hours required.\n\n(d) Qualifying duties shall include the following:\n\n(1) Health education;\n\n(2) Coordinating care including referrals;\n\n(3) Informal support or counseling, or both;\n\n(4) Advocacy for individuals or communities, or both;\n\n(5) Assessment of community needs or individual needs, or both;\n\n(6) Activities to increase community capacity or individual capacity, or both;\n\n(7) Disease prevention and management; and\n\n(8) Outreach.\n\n(e) An individual who engaged in other duties in addition to qualifying duties shall count only those hours spent on qualifying duties towards the total hours required.\n\nSource. #14388, eff 10-24-25, EXPIRES: 10-24-35",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/plc2000.html"
}
